Scope: flat-space scalar wave equation. In spherical symmetry, the massless scalar wave equation: ∂_t²φ = ∂_r²φ + (2/r)∂_rφ (flat space, no gravity). Or 1+1D Cartesian: ∂_t²φ = ∂_x²φ. The class is AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH (spherically symmetric scalar field), so a spherically symmetric flat-space wave test is the right calibration: the reduced equation with the 2/r term or the 1+1D reduction using ψ = rφ satisfying ∂_t²ψ = ∂_r²ψ.

